# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# NOT-4 and NOT-9: the empty log takes the whole screen, and gives every
# pixel of it back.
#
# **A single leg, and it has to be one.** The obvious form is a pair —
# run it with the seam off and diff — and it cannot work here, for a
# reason worth writing down rather than discovering twice. The key that
# opens the log reaches the program in the seam-off run, where the
# adventuring bar answers an unknown letter by stepping its own
# highlight. From that moment the two runs differ on the bar row
# whatever the give-back does, and the difference measured is the
# highlight rather than the journal (#234).
#
# So the give-back is stated directly instead, and more strongly: the
# frame after the log closes is the same screen as the frame before it
# opened.
about the log takes the whole screen and gives every pixel of it back
kind single
program START.EXE
store tests/visual/reader-store.txt
both code-wheel
# The code-wheel bypass is gated on the wheel itself (#115), and both
# sides of this pair drive past the challenge, so both need it. Pinned
# by digest because a document never enters this tree.
document 0db301aeac4d2ec1e63b409ca6d3c9d39c63381d6712ff2ce7edc0528c6586fd
seam journal
until 260000000
every 25

key A@7601
key Return@7651
key L@8951
key A@9201
key N@10600
key Escape@11400

rect bar 0,190,319,199

# The log up, holding still, with nothing pressed.
same 10800-11375

# And the screen before it, back again after it: viewport, roster,
# status line, ornaments, every pixel — **except the bar row**, and that
# exception is a finding rather than a convenience.
#
# What comes back on the bar is the right bar, in the right place, with
# the right words. What does not come back is *which of them the
# highlight is sitting on*: the give-back injects a space to make the
# menu-bar routine return and draw itself again, and the routine draws
# itself with the highlight at its first command. A player who had
# stepped it along finds it back at the start after using the journal.
#
# Measured here (#234): before the log and after it, 951 pixels differ
# and every one of them is on the bar row. NOT-2's leg is what asserts
# the bar itself.
equal 10600 11800 bar
